WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.220
Did you ever wonder about that closed door

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:06.660
in Cathedral Ward? You know the one, it's below the church giant with the ball and chain

00:00:06.879 --> 00:00:09.239
and past the room where you rolled through all the pots

00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:12.869
It's the sort of door you forget about even if you finish the game

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:18.090
But think about it now You never open that door. Did you? Well, you're not alone?

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:24.020
No one's opened this door yet and perhaps. No one ever will but we do know where it leads

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:24.900
The cliff we're on

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:31.469
Overlooks the Great bridge where we fought the Cleric Beast and it's no great leap of logic to assume this door is the same door

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.890
as the one at the end of the bridge

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:40.259
But what is interesting to note is that From Software actually put the effort in to make these two doors align perfectly in the world

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:45.360
Let's prove it. Go over to the door and throw down a couple of shining coins- actually throw 40

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:50.429
This is the only time in the game these are useful go crazy with it then run all the way to the great bridge without

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.559
Reloading your game and the door at the end

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:59.128
Will have your shining coins on it still. Which proves that these parts of the world are connected in both the lore and physically

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:04.228
Chances are you could probably unlock this shortcut once upon a time, but in the game's current state

00:01:04.228 --> 00:01:08.500
It doesn't make much sense for it to exist so they must have only removed half of it.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.840
While we're in Central Yharnam

